WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.542
Now translate familiar Python control flow into Lang Graph.

00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:08.827
A Python dictionary becomes typed graph state.

00:00:08.827 --> 00:00:11.457
A function becomes a node.

00:00:11.457 --> 00:00:16.437
An if or else branch becomes a conditional edge or a command.

00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:20.302
A while loop becomes a cycle between nodes.

00:00:20.302 --> 00:00:23.128
A break becomes a transition to end.

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:30.226
This translation is important because Lang Graph is not introducing a completely different programming concept.

00:00:30.226 --> 00:00:34.111
It is making the control flow explicit and inspectable.

00:00:34.111 --> 00:00:41.656
For example, instead of a while loop that calls retrieve, grade, and rewrite, you may have three nodes connected in a

00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:42.925
cycle.

00:00:43.705 --> 00:00:49.394
If you can point to the matching Python idea, you understand the graph at the right level.
